WEBVTT

00:07.030 --> 00:08.510
What was that noise?

00:10.610 --> 00:12.150
What...

00:13.270 --> 00:16.530
Ibara, you have the right to remain silent!

00:21.510 --> 00:24.030
I've always wanted to say that.

00:24.650 --> 00:27.710
<i>I shot one of the remaining bullets 
in the air and the other at Moz.</i>

00:27.710 --> 00:30.130
<i>Which means the last one...</i>

00:30.780 --> 00:33.390
Anything you say can be 
used against you in...

00:33.390 --> 00:34.780
What comes after that again?

00:34.780 --> 00:37.450
Battery? Obstruction of something-something?

00:37.450 --> 00:40.140
I dunno. Whatever.

00:40.500 --> 00:43.730
You're under arrest on 
suspicion of being bad!

00:55.530 --> 00:59.710
The Medusa's mine!

02:31.270 --> 02:36.010
<b>Flicker of Doom</b>

02:47.690 --> 02:49.290
We've got the ultimate weapon!

02:49.290 --> 02:50.750
Doesn't that mean we've won?

02:50.750 --> 02:52.940
Your boy Yo here's done good!

02:53.210 --> 02:57.650
All I need to do is hit that 
annoying bastard who insta-KO'd me

02:57.650 --> 03:00.130
with the petrification beam!

03:00.610 --> 03:02.950
Petrification beam!

03:04.770 --> 03:06.750
That's it for the enemy!

03:06.750 --> 03:08.090
You're amazing!

03:08.090 --> 03:11.030
Yo-kun's the leader of the 
Kingdom of Science! It's settled!

03:11.030 --> 03:13.540
I'm exhilarated by Yo-kun's skills.

03:17.590 --> 03:19.340
Take this, Moz!

03:20.030 --> 03:22.340
Petrification beam!

03:30.010 --> 03:33.440
<i>I have no idea how to use it.</i>

03:38.490 --> 03:40.790
Hyoga...

03:40.790 --> 03:43.450
You're strong for sure, but...

03:44.080 --> 03:47.950
The way you handle your 
spear reeks of effort.

03:47.950 --> 03:51.710
I can smell the sweat of all 
the practice you put into it.

03:56.010 --> 03:57.620
Too bad.

03:57.620 --> 04:00.020
You'll never beat me like that.

04:00.610 --> 04:03.490
I'm a genius, after all.

04:03.970 --> 04:08.110
Unlike your false fangs 
put together with practice,

04:09.130 --> 04:12.060
I was born the strongest.

04:22.680 --> 04:24.200
<i>He didn't fall.</i>

04:24.590 --> 04:26.700
<i>He escaped into the water.</i>

04:46.170 --> 04:49.930
<i>Look at him, desperately 
tucking tail and running away.</i>

04:49.930 --> 04:51.890
<i>Pathetic.</i>

04:57.180 --> 04:58.070
<i>Indeed...</i>

04:58.070 --> 05:01.830
<i>Senku-kun isn't the kind of man 
who would tuck tail and run.</i>

05:03.160 --> 05:06.740
<i>Which means they're out looking for...</i>

05:12.870 --> 05:14.620
Isn't this...

05:15.000 --> 05:19.880
<i>The almighty weapon for me, 
the trump card of might.</i>

05:23.950 --> 05:26.480
<i>I believe he'll make it for me.</i>

05:26.990 --> 05:28.720
<i>I believe in him.</i>

05:31.140 --> 05:32.470
<i>Believe?</i>

05:33.040 --> 05:35.730
<i>Me? In Senku and the others?</i>

05:46.980 --> 05:49.430
Kinro, your golden spear.

05:49.740 --> 05:51.910
Do you remember how thick it is?

05:53.070 --> 05:56.290
Some of these are close, but it'll be tight.

05:56.590 --> 06:00.070
You aren't gonna just find 
one that's the perfect fit.

06:01.310 --> 06:03.460
Graphite. Basically, chimney soot.

06:03.460 --> 06:09.000
Throw some alcohol on it, 
and you get some quick lubricant.

06:11.050 --> 06:12.880
Mecha-Senku here!

06:12.880 --> 06:14.790
It's been a while, huh?

06:14.790 --> 06:18.700
Carbon crystals have super slippery surfaces.

06:14.790 --> 06:21.650
<b>Dry Lubricant</b>

06:18.700 --> 06:21.650
You can even get by with pencil lead.

06:21.650 --> 06:26.620
Give a stubborn drawer some work with 
a pencil, and it'll be butter smooth!

06:26.620 --> 06:29.310
But it'll turn your hand 
all black if you touch it,

06:29.310 --> 06:32.120
so be sure to tell your family first.

06:36.490 --> 06:37.940
This is incredible!

06:37.940 --> 06:40.410
Slippery shiny!

06:44.830 --> 06:47.290
Long, long ago,

06:47.290 --> 06:50.480
we had our strongest guy, Magma-chan,

06:50.480 --> 06:54.470
toss a rock for us so we could 
pretend we'd invented

06:54.470 --> 06:57.350
the ultimate weapon that is the gun.

06:57.640 --> 06:59.880
It won't be a casual toss this time.

06:59.880 --> 07:03.360
Can we trust your brute 
force to make it, Magma?

07:05.260 --> 07:08.560
Do you know who I am, you weaklings?

07:18.740 --> 07:20.600
Thank you very much.

07:20.600 --> 07:22.940
You are indeed quite proper.

07:24.460 --> 07:28.620
Allow me to show you, Moz-kun, 
the spear of science.

07:29.210 --> 07:34.220
Witness five hundred years 
of Owari Kanryu-style.

07:39.370 --> 07:41.860
<i>How is his spear moving like that?</i>

07:42.180 --> 07:43.790
<i>Like a round moon...</i>

07:44.620 --> 07:45.690
<i>No!</i>

07:46.570 --> 07:48.400
<i>A golden light!</i>

07:48.400 --> 07:49.820
<i>Sunlight!</i>

07:54.860 --> 07:55.990
Impossible!

07:55.990 --> 07:57.550
It's too fast!

07:57.550 --> 07:59.340
It isn't moving like a spear!

07:59.340 --> 08:00.910
How is this possible?

08:01.130 --> 08:03.670
Basically, it's leverage.

08:04.640 --> 08:06.170
I'm using the barrel as a support.

08:07.200 --> 08:10.850
It takes quite a few years to master.

08:10.850 --> 08:15.930
The kudayari made by the Kingdom 
of Science works delightfully well.

08:16.150 --> 08:19.660
Shit, the kudayari's the best weapon ever!

08:19.660 --> 08:21.000
Look at Moz!

08:22.600 --> 08:24.440
Freaking hell!

08:24.440 --> 08:26.900
Damn this sorcery weapon!

08:29.130 --> 08:32.440
Sorcery weapon, you say?

08:33.560 --> 08:39.070
What do you think is the strongest 
weapon of all, Moz-kun?

08:41.280 --> 08:44.710
It's what sets the human 
species apart from all else...

08:46.920 --> 08:49.920
The ability to build upon past generations.

08:53.570 --> 08:54.770
Again.

08:54.770 --> 08:55.760
Yes, sir.

08:56.800 --> 09:04.810
<b>Hard Work Will Be Rewarded</b>

08:57.980 --> 09:04.450
Diligent work done over thousands of years.

09:13.130 --> 09:17.080
We continue to refine, 
and even through death,

09:17.080 --> 09:19.960
carry our work through 
to the next generation.

09:23.850 --> 09:30.010
No one genius is going to single-handedly 
defeat such tireless refinement.

09:33.880 --> 09:34.780
Shoo!

09:34.780 --> 09:36.970
I'mma pew-pew you with my sorcery!

09:38.430 --> 09:40.290
<i>Not that I have any more ammo.</i>

09:40.870 --> 09:43.560
Ah, well. I don't know how to use this thing.

09:43.560 --> 09:47.020
Guess I'll hold on to it so I can at least 
keep the island from getting petrified.

09:47.020 --> 09:49.810
Three meters. One second.

10:12.630 --> 10:15.550
What's going on here?!

10:15.550 --> 10:16.890
<i>Oarashi!</i>

10:16.890 --> 10:19.850
<i>I should hand him the petrification 
device immediately!</i>

10:19.850 --> 10:21.440
<i>No, let's not rush.</i>

10:21.440 --> 10:26.680
<i>This old man's strong because he's 
especially cautious at times like these.</i>

10:26.680 --> 10:31.270
<i>Oarashi's already seen how 
terrifying this thing can be.</i>

10:31.670 --> 10:38.570
<i>The best way to make sure he's </i>forced<i> 
to take it to the middle of the island...</i>

10:41.980 --> 10:46.080
<i>Two thousand meters. Fifteen minutes.</i>

11:04.290 --> 11:05.430
<i>I heard that!</i>

11:05.640 --> 11:08.250
<i>Meters... and seconds?</i>

11:08.250 --> 11:10.940
<i>And the twisted sound of petrification!</i>

11:15.210 --> 11:18.120
He's running with a furious look on his face.

11:18.120 --> 11:19.390
Oarashi?

11:20.090 --> 11:22.610
Everyone on the island 
knows where he's going.

11:22.610 --> 11:24.620
That road leads to the center of the island!

11:24.840 --> 11:26.230
Please, Taiju!

11:26.230 --> 11:29.480
Use your powerful voice to let everyone know!

11:30.040 --> 11:35.460
That man, Oarashi, has the Medusa!

11:36.000 --> 11:38.130
He's going to engulf the island!

11:38.130 --> 11:39.580
Stop him!

12:00.490 --> 12:05.090
I don't know what's going on, 
but protect Oarashi-sama!

12:05.660 --> 12:06.990
Wrong team! Wrong team!

12:06.990 --> 12:08.990
He's going to get you petrified, too!

12:12.330 --> 12:13.610
Yes!

12:16.190 --> 12:21.350
Miracle power!

12:24.040 --> 12:30.770
No one's got more brute 
strength than Oarashi.

12:31.240 --> 12:32.980
<i>What now, then?</i>

12:32.980 --> 12:35.060
<i>We don't have time to escape to sea now!</i>

12:35.060 --> 12:36.490
<i>Think...</i>

12:36.490 --> 12:38.230
<i>What can we do?</i>

12:38.610 --> 12:41.360
<i>What can I do?</i>

12:42.060 --> 12:43.250
<i>Right...</i>

12:43.250 --> 12:44.610
<i>I'm the explorer...</i>

12:44.610 --> 12:46.410
<i>Science user Chrome!</i>

12:46.730 --> 12:50.960
<i>Senku said science is all about repeatability.</i>

12:50.960 --> 12:52.000
<i>Think!</i>

12:52.000 --> 12:53.790
<i>Remember the last petrification beam!</i>

12:55.450 --> 12:59.770
<i>We weren't just standing 
there watching for nothing!</i>

13:02.420 --> 13:12.100
Senku, last time I let that damn 
light get me, I had a front row seat.

13:14.470 --> 13:19.230
I was measuring how the 
petrification beam grows.

13:22.090 --> 13:25.510
It's always the same speed!

13:30.760 --> 13:33.180
Looks like you've come up with 
something. Tell us, Chrome!

13:33.180 --> 13:34.090
Sure did!

13:34.090 --> 13:36.080
I've got the sickest, most disgusting plan.

13:37.660 --> 13:39.610
No one in the Kingdom of Science

13:39.610 --> 13:44.180
would hesitate to make a pathetic 
move if it let us move forward!

13:57.850 --> 13:59.460
How is he so powerful?

13:59.460 --> 14:02.470
Damn it, I'm almost there!

14:02.470 --> 14:04.290
Take the petrification weapon from him!

14:04.290 --> 14:06.320
We have to throw it far away!

14:07.680 --> 14:09.980
H-He doesn't have anything!

14:10.320 --> 14:11.320
Why?!

14:12.070 --> 14:13.930
Get off me!

14:13.930 --> 14:20.330
Ibara-sama told me that I won't be 
petrified if I go to the middle of the island!

14:22.350 --> 14:24.290
<i>I'm swallowing water!</i>

14:28.070 --> 14:34.100
So, to avoid getting petrified, 
you have to go to the middle of the island.

14:34.100 --> 14:36.810
You'd better hurry!

14:43.290 --> 14:45.700
This can't be!

15:08.910 --> 15:11.370
We're counting on you, Senku!

15:12.730 --> 15:14.280
You guys...

15:14.850 --> 15:18.730
Senku, you're the only one 
who can take on the Medusa!

15:18.730 --> 15:21.750
Use your science thinking power!

15:24.170 --> 15:29.220
The Kingdom of Science is going all-in 
to shut down the petrification beam!

15:34.360 --> 15:35.520
Everyone!

15:35.520 --> 15:38.000
Everyone on the island is 
going to get petrified!

15:39.930 --> 15:42.890
<i>I need to at least share 
the information I acquired!</i>

15:43.680 --> 15:45.590
The petrification beam is activated by

15:45.590 --> 15:47.460
voicing the effective range 
and countdown time!

15:54.970 --> 15:56.270
It's over.

15:56.270 --> 15:57.720
For both of us.

15:58.090 --> 16:00.010
It appears so.

16:01.190 --> 16:06.660
You and I are both are too 
dangerous for either force.

16:06.660 --> 16:09.190
I doubt we will ever be 
released from petrification.

16:09.870 --> 16:14.100
Well, shit, my first defeat is the end of me.

16:15.060 --> 16:18.250
If we ever are released...

16:18.250 --> 16:23.490
I'm interested in those hundreds of years 
of refinement you were talking about.

16:23.490 --> 16:25.750
Your so-called kudayari.

16:26.590 --> 16:28.050
That's fine with me.

16:28.500 --> 16:35.760
The Owari Kanryu-style keeps its doors 
open to all who will partake properly.

18:06.740 --> 18:10.030
This is hilarious! I won all by myself!

18:10.030 --> 18:14.190
I'm actually the last one on this island!

18:16.030 --> 18:20.680
Oh, dear, her luscious figure is all rock!

18:20.680 --> 18:22.480
How sad.

18:22.480 --> 18:24.850
Not a problem, though!

18:24.850 --> 18:31.210
The old man knows that the sorcery 
people have revival water!

18:31.210 --> 18:35.860
And if I don't have enough, I'll torture 
someone to force them to make more!

18:35.860 --> 18:40.800
They were all chasing after Oarashi, 
so it'll be easy enough to find them.

18:49.020 --> 18:50.850
<i>They've formed a line?</i>

18:50.850 --> 18:54.300
<i>And they've all taken on the 
same stone pose for some reason.</i>

19:04.790 --> 19:06.490
This face...

19:21.180 --> 19:23.500
You saw...

19:23.500 --> 19:26.150
Though you were just a baby...

19:26.830 --> 19:30.880
For generations, the Master has 
married women with strong memory,

19:30.880 --> 19:32.940
so they can pass down the hundred tales.

19:33.450 --> 19:34.710
Soyuz...

19:34.710 --> 19:37.280
This child's memory is 
astounding just the same!

19:41.080 --> 19:43.390
How could you, Ibara-sama?!

19:44.410 --> 19:45.260
Catch them!

19:45.260 --> 19:47.790
Prince Soyuz has been abducted!

19:48.140 --> 19:50.000
Hold it!

20:05.790 --> 20:08.930
Too bad, Soyuz-chan!

20:08.930 --> 20:13.440
After twenty years of hard living, 
and then coming all the way back...

20:13.440 --> 20:19.970
You can sleep forever as a 
statue with your goofy daddy.

20:40.370 --> 20:42.020
<i>Footprints?</i>

20:44.570 --> 20:46.580
<i>Odd, isn't it?</i>

20:46.580 --> 20:51.060
<i>They couldn't have gotten so far, 
running from the petrification beam.</i>

20:59.480 --> 21:02.550
Was that sound...

21:03.280 --> 21:06.070
<i>The same as the one coming from the earring?</i>

21:19.120 --> 21:22.460
<i>The beast that escaped from the ship?</i>

21:26.570 --> 21:29.230
<i>No! It's not a living creature!</i>

21:29.230 --> 21:31.600
<i>Is it their sorcery?</i>

21:34.250 --> 21:36.940
<i>Five meters. One second.</i>

21:45.620 --> 21:48.910
Damn, did Ukyo get it wrong?

21:48.910 --> 21:53.660
Nah, I guess it doesn't work 
unless you talk at it up close.

21:55.060 --> 21:57.160
Yo, Ibara.

21:58.820 --> 22:01.500
Guess it's just the two of us.

22:01.860 --> 22:07.510
Time for our happy science versus 
Medusa one-on-one boss fight.

22:07.990 --> 22:12.890
How the hell are you alive?!

23:52.030 --> 23:54.990
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:54.990 --> 24:00.000
<b>This is a work of fiction, but the plants, 
animals, and production methods described are based on reality.
Foraging and making things on your own accord is extremely dangerous
and, in some cases, illegal. Please do not imitate without expertise.</b>
